From b3489f3b2e2c645606e6bcb4d7b23c5f0bc00cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dalton Singleton <blumoon94@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:47:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Haiku keyboard and mouse backend

Haiku only accepts input events from input_server device add-ons, so the
backend forwards keyboard, text and mouse events over a named kernel port
to a small add-on (virtualhid_input) that enqueues them like a physical
keyboard and mouse. The user's keymap (including dead keys), lock keys,
mouse and click settings apply.

- haiku_backend.cpp: Backend implementation for keyboards and mice; only
  uses kernel ports, so the library itself needs no Haiku kit library
- haiku_keycodes.cpp: Windows virtual-key to Haiku key code table, derived
  from Haiku's HID keyboard driver
- haiku_input_protocol.hpp: versioned fixed-size event protocol shared with
  the add-on; the add-on validates every message against its size
- input_server/: the add-on (option LIBVIRTUALHID_BUILD_HAIKU_INPUT_ADDON).
  It merges bursts of relative motion and spaces pointer events so
  input_server applies each to the current cursor position, and releases
  held keys and buttons separately when a keyboard or mouse closes.

Gamepads, touch and pen tablets report as not implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
